[Music]  as we told you earlier the weekend's  mass shootings in ohio and texas have  renewed calls for gun control  legislation  president trump talked about gun  violence and ideological hatred this  morning so let's discuss it with a key  member of congress south carolina  senator lindsey graham chair of the  judiciary committee he joins us from  greenville south carolina welcome  senator  thank you for having me i'm here at the  greenville gop we had a  good talk tonight about a lot of things  yeah we're going to try to do that with  you as well i first want to get your  reaction to the weekend's  um events and of course as predictable  plenty of reaction on both sides of the  aisle that's political in nature  well number one the people to blame are  the shooters and nobody else is a sick  and senseless crime and  there's a common pattern in many of  these cases people are disturbed they  take the law in their own hands they're  full of hate and  they act out and it's time for us to act  you know calling the president names is  not going to solve this problem  for the last 24 hours it's been really  over the top  i'm looking for a democrat to work with  not to insult  so i'm hoping i can find some democrats  that will work with me  starting with the idea of red flag laws  i think these  protective orders have a lot of hope to  solve some of these cases  well i want to put up a map now so folks  can see where there are a number of  states that have done this across the  country of course there are always  concerns about due process a lot of  people have  that guns could be taken second  amendment rights could be potentially  violated before people have a chance to  make their side of the case  how do you thread that needle well  number one  indiana was one of the first states to  do this  here's what we do this is not going to  be a federal law to be a federal grant  program  to get the federal grant you have to  have due process  there has to be an imminent threat of  harm to oneself  or to others before the police and it  can only be the police can go to a judge  you have a hearing you gotta have more  likely than not standard  there's an imminent threat of bodily  injury seven days later you have a  full-blown hearing  clear and convincing evidence where the  gun owner can come in and defend  themselves and the government has to  prove  by clear and convincing evidence that  their the person is disturbed a danger  to themselves of others  and if that test is met they can seize  the guns and get the person the help  they need  in in parkland florida cruz had 32 to 40  visits by the cops  they had no way to stop him he did  everything but take an ad  out in the paper or kill people so what  i want to do is encourage these laws  with robust due process  and i think that's the president's goal  also well he talked about that today he  talked about trying to unify  and make this a not a partisan issue but  to find bipartisan solutions on the hill  that's been really tough to do i want to  play something from former democratic  congressman luis gutierrez today  talking about first the discussion was  in the context of the war on terror and  he says it's really the domestic issue  we have to look at  and he's not buying what the president  was selling today here's what he said  yes we need a war a war on  terrorism here in the united states of  america  to eradicate but the first thing we need  to do is the president of the united  states  has to stop has to stop igniting the  flames of hatred and bigotry  and division in this country i don't  believe any of what you said today  senator where is the bipartisan space to  get something done  well i've worked with senator blumenthal  and we're getting close we're going to  run it by the white house we've talked  to gun owning owner group so we talked  to the cops  and we're trying to come up with a  serious solution to a serious problem  we're trying to empower police officers  to do something before it's too late  with plenty of due process we're not  trying to take anybody's guns away from  them  we're trying to get guns out of the  hands of people who are dangerous  who actually may kill themselves or  somebody else that's the goal we're  trying to shut down these social media  sites  that spew hate we're trying to find  solutions and for the last 24 hours it's  been pretty  disappointing to hear all the rhetoric  directed at president trump  president trump is not the problem here  the congress for years has been talking  it's now time to act  and if senator blumenthal and i can come  up with a package  that has protections for the gun owner  but allows the cops to do something  before it's too late i hope we get a  vote in the senate and it will pass  okay i want to ask you about some  foreign policy issues as well while we  have you  the president last week talking about  the fact that listen he campaigned on  bringing our troops home from a number  of conflicts around the world  he's now talking about afghanistan you  had some strong  cautions for him but here's what he said  about bringing those folks home from  afghanistan  we've been there 19 years we're not  really  um let's put it this way we're more  policemen than anything else  and that's not for our soldiers we could  win the war in afghanistan  in less than a week but i'm not looking  to kill 10 million  people and i'm not talking nuclear what  are your concerns about bringing  everyone home all u.s  operations from that area every  commander i've talked to  the intelligence community says that  al-qaeda and  isis are re-emerging in afghanistan that  if we draw all  if we withdraw all of our forces they  can hit us in the region and here at  home  this is exactly what they told president  obama  it is not right to right to leave if  we'd had a  residual force in iraq there would be no  isis isis has now moved to afghanistan  along with al qaeda  my belief is that a small  counterterrorism force  will protect the american homeland from  another 911  it's just not me saying that it is the  intelligence community and every  military commander  president trump has done a great job of  rebuilding the military he's gone after  isis and syria and iraq  we've got their foot on we've got our  foot on their throat if we pull  all of our troops out it will we just  matter of time in my view  do they regenerate the good news is a  very small counterterrorism force  is an insurance policy against another  911  and i hope the president will see it  that way and follow the advice of his  commanders and if he gets in the debate  with joe biden here's what i would  recommend the president to do aren't you  the guy that gave us isis aren't you the  guy that told  uh we're getting out no matter what the  military says mr president don't go down  the joe biden barack obama road when it  comes to afghanistan  this is where the whole thing started  and we got to get afghanistan right in  the good news  is with a few thousand counter-terrorism  forces we can protect america  for a very long time to come and we can  reduce the cost  and we should reduce the cost all right  senator lindsey graham live from  greenville south carolina tonight thank  you sir  thank you

